Name: tls_eccurve
Type: STRING
Default-Value: X25519MLKEM768:X25519:prime256v1:secp384r1
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

Colon-separated list of the groups (elliptic curves and hybrid
post-quantum key exchanges) offered for ECDHE, most preferred first.
Groups this build of OpenSSL doesn't support are skipped.  See
'openssl list -tls-groups' for possible values.

A TLS 1.3 client guesses which group the server will take and sends a key
share for it up front.  If the server offers none of the client's guesses,
it answers with a HelloRetryRequest, which costs an extra round trip on
every connection and rules out 0-RTT early data, so keep the groups
popular clients lead with (X25519MLKEM768 and X25519) near the front.
